 **Verification, not deployment:** migrated a populated disposable PostgreSQL copy and checked every retained column/row on all 130 surviving application tables against its pre-migration contents. Reloaded all 13 development archive CSVs into typed scratch tables and compared both directions with the source projections. A held writer and an unexpected incoming FK each aborted the migration without a partial drop. A warm release-1 connection returned identical visible records across cutover. Migration and request specs exercise NULLs, a quoted tenant schema, multiline CSV, an unwritable archive, drift and shared readers with the post-migration schema. The final two targeted runs passed 632 examples, including English i18n, legislation proposals, debates, polls and investments.
 
-## Handoff for release 3 — wait for release 2 shipment confirmation
+## Handoff from release 2 (historical checklist)
 
-**All shared-row cleanup is outstanding.** Capture fresh preimages under `db/` before deleting or changing anything. Keep attachment bytes (including versions/variants where applicable) before any purge. Use the **successful release-2 archive for that tenant**, not absent columns or guessed IDs. In particular `proposals.csv` maps proposals to communities; `linked_map_locations.csv` identifies map rows that lost their link. Recheck current investment ownership before deleting either. Keep ordinary questions formerly linked to proposals; use `polls.related_type` to identify dashboard polls, not the archived question links.
+**At the end of release 2, all shared-row cleanup was outstanding.** Capture fresh preimages under `db/` before deleting or changing anything. Keep attachment bytes (including versions/variants where applicable) before any purge. Use the **successful release-2 archive for that tenant**, not absent columns or guessed IDs. In particular `proposals.csv` maps proposals to communities; `linked_map_locations.csv` identifies map rows that lost their link. Recheck current investment ownership before deleting either. Keep ordinary questions formerly linked to proposals; use `polls.related_type` to identify dashboard polls, not the archived question links.
 
 1. Inventory and archive typed rows by **exact type** (`Proposal`, `ProposalNotification`, `Dashboard::Action`, `Dashboard::ExecutedAction`, `Dashboard::AdministratorTask`), never a substring like `%Proposal%` and never numeric ID alone. Known live references at inspection included `comments.commentable_type`, `votes.votable_type`, `follows.followable_type`, `flags.flaggable_type`, `activities.actionable_type`, `notifications.notifiable_type`, both ends of `related_contents`, `taggings.taggable_type`, `polls.related_type` and dashboard task sources. Check even empty tables: signature sheets/signatures, milestone and progress owners, document/image/link owners, ML summaries, remote translations, reports, SDG relations/reviews, audit and Active Storage records. Inspect the actual catalog for additional FKs and polymorphic pairs. The identifying columns are now in the release-2 archive.
 2. Trace second-order dependencies, not just type columns: comment translations/replies, votes/flags/notifications/activities on those comments, opposite related-content rows and scores, attachments, proposal-only communities and their topics/comments, and dashboard polls and their descendants. Check for shared owners before removal. Preserve city/budget polls, their questions (including those previously copied from proposals), investment communities, legislation proposals and all unrelated rows. Do not just null a dashboard poll's `related_type` and thereby publish it. Reconcile affected counter caches without resetting unrelated data. Order cleanup/transactions so the serving release never sees a child whose parent it must render is gone.
 3. Include obsolete settings (except the three shared keys above), `widget_feeds`, `web_sections`/banner sections, stored proposal-only customization text and recipient segments. Review operator-authored links/cards, queued work and generated ML/sitemap files rather than erasing arbitrary content containing the word “proposal”. Check every tenant for dangling direct **and indirect** references and check surviving data against the backup. Only after the data/schema migration is confirmed everywhere remove `ignored_columns` and now-unnecessary legacy guards. If cleanup runs while release 2 is serving, keep any guard it relies on valid for the entire overlap. Retain all dumps and record what actually shipped here.
+
+## Release 3 — final deploy, ready to ship
+
+The operator confirmed releases 1 and 2 are on every server. `consul_development.public` is at `20260829120000`. **Release 3 has not been applied to that database.** Its migration `20260830120000` changes rows, not the schema. The old release can keep querying every table and column it uses, including `polls.related_type`. Do **not** start release-3 web servers or workers before migration succeeds everywhere: their queries no longer hide legacy rows.
+
+### What the cleanup does
+
+* Starts with exact retired Rails type names and the release-2 archive, not title text, substrings, or IDs shared across types. Builds the dependent set to a fixed point with SQL (including hidden rows, comment ancestry, opposite relations and poll descendants). Checks the catalog for unreviewed polymorphic pairs and cascading FK actions. Removes only archived rows, child first, in one transaction per schema.
+* Removes proposal-only communities, their topics and discussions, and former proposal map locations. Rechecks current owners including hidden investments and legislation proposals. Dashboard polls are deleted, **not made public**. The cleanup never uses a copied question's former `proposal_id` as a reason to delete it. Shared geozones, officers, booths, investments, city/budget polls, `Legislation::Proposal`, their participants and their data stay.
+* Reconciles notification and tagging counters for affected owners only. Clears obsolete signature/paper-ballot links on otherwise surviving votes/ballots. Removes the 17 retired settings, not the three shared legislation settings. Removes obsolete feed/section rows, their owned records and proposal-script ML metadata, not every banner, tag or ML result. Clears the two retired mail recipient selections to **no recipients**, retaining authored messages and delivery history; never substitutes a wider audience.
+* Removes overrides of retired translation keys by exact key and strips only known, seeded permission list items and shortcut rows from the three welcome pages and accessibility page. Does not overwrite pages from seeds, rewrite local prose, or prune Spanish locale files. Do not mass-delete content, audit history, links or jobs by keyword. Non-shipped locales may still have old wording in otherwise live links to the home page; those are translations, not proposal records.
+* Removes the release-1 `ignored_columns`, temporary reader scopes and tag callback exception from the new app. Shared endpoints still reject unsupported resource types; legislation routes, settings and shared styling remain. Historical migrations, including both archive writers, stay with the app.
+
+### Copies and checks during preparation
+
+The retained release-2 migration archive here is `db/citizen_proposal_archives/20261119T192816Z-017b708c-01f0-4482-9756-7c75dd002f32/` (same manifest checksum and data as the earlier preparation snapshot). A fresh repeatable-read snapshot of release-3 **preimages** from the deployment database is in:
+
+`db/citizen_proposal_archives/20261119T195340Z-51e7fbc3-baa6-4769-a8e2-f762074e5fd5/`
+
+`manifest.json` SHA-256: `b819afb32dca3635657a48cc37dafc94391f31ce217ec043dc69aced0997150f`. Only temporary planning tables were written; the transaction was rolled back. The 63 CSV files include full rows, stable IDs, row counts and checksums (including empty selections); `update_*` files contain the **before** rows of edits. `source.json` identifies the release-2 input. These private files contain citizen information, including user data. Keep them off the web and out of Git, on the durable protected archive volume. No original archive is replaced.
+
+At inspection the plan had **169 deletes and 167 edits**. This included 14 comments with their translations, 56 votes, 12 follows, 5 notifications, 12 communities, 1 topic, 2 maps, and 1 dashboard poll with its question and options. Edits were 4 user counters, 3 tag counters and 160 stored page translations. There were no tenant schemas, attachment links, delayed jobs, banners/cards, newsletters, admin announcements or ML jobs to resolve in this database. No citizen-proposal export or route was found in the generated ML data directory or sitemaps here. These are observations, not hardcoded deployment counts.
+
+On a disposable PostgreSQL copy, compared **all 130 application tables**: every archived preimage matched the source, all 169 deleted IDs were absent, and surviving rows and columns matched except for the intended edits. Checked the resulting counters. A held writer aborted a migration without any partial deletes; after retry, a warm release-2 process continued to read notifications, activity, votes, follows, comments and polls across the commit. Tests include shared map/community ownership, same-numbered legislation records, city questions, soft-hidden discussions, shared attachment bytes, customized text, a damaged or foreign archive, and a new reference added after backup. Targeted suites passed (719 examples, then 203 including the attachment case; final migration, endpoint and English i18n check: 14 examples).
+
+### To ship — give these steps to hosting
+
+1. **Leave release 2 serving.** Confirm the target, release-2 version, and tenant list again. Verify recoverable database and attachment-storage snapshots (including variants and versions). Keep the original archives and mount `db/citizen_proposal_archives/` as in release 2. Check external schedules, queued/retry jobs, live ML processes, custom links/cards and generated files for retired targets. Drain relevant jobs with compatible workers; don't purge the queue or storage. If there are generated proposal exports on a host, archive privately before taking them off the web. Retain unrelated files. No reseed.
+2. Match each tenant to the archive in its **successful release-2 migration log**. Do not choose the latest directory, a rehearsal or the release-3 preparation copy. Compare the manifest and files with the retained backup. For the inspected installation the migration environment is:
+
+   ```sh
+   cd /app
+   export CITIZEN_PROPOSAL_RELEASE2_ARCHIVES='{"public":"20261119T192816Z-017b708c-01f0-4482-9756-7c75dd002f32"}'
+   RAILS_ENV=development bin/rails db:migrate
+   ```
+
+   With a different archive log or more tenants, use their verified directory names keyed by exact schema name. Pass the variable to the **migration process**, not just the web servers. If the selection includes Active Storage attachments, also supply `CITIZEN_PROPOSAL_STORAGE_BACKUP` with the non-secret identifier of the verified immutable storage snapshot. The migration never invokes purge, deletes shared blobs/variants or touches stored bytes. The backup protects detached files even against later external storage garbage collection.
+3. Migration writes and reads back a **new** private archive before taking write locks. It locks without waiting, rebuilds the selection under lock, verifies live preimages against the dump and checks mutation counts. Readers can continue; the write phase has short timeouts and a time budget. A bad/missing archive, unexpected dependency, ambiguous owner, drift, or contention means **stop; don't switch traffic**. Leave release 2 up, correct the cause and retry; do not force a cascade, bypass checks or stretch lock timeouts. Repeated time-budget failures need a batched plan. A failed attempt's archive is not proof that its transaction committed.
+4. Confirm `20260830120000` is `up` in `public` and **every tenant**. Record each successful release-3 archive path, verify its manifest/checksums on the retained volume, and copy it to protected backup storage. For a recovery drill load the CSVs into scratch tables using the release-2 schema and PostgreSQL `COPY ... CSV HEADER` as above: deletion files contain entire rows; use the `update_*` rows by ID and only the changed fields. Do not load snapshots over live users or undo later votes/edits.
+5. Now roll release-3 web servers and workers. Check former participants' profiles/notifications, debate commenting/voting, city poll questions, investments/communities, legislation proposals and moderation in English and Spanish. `/proposals` and the author dashboard must stay unavailable. Refresh normal sitemaps. If the new app fails, **roll back code only to release 2**; its filters are harmless on the cleaned data. Do not run `db:rollback` or deploy the pre-removal code.
+
+**Left to do:** ship and verify this release, record the successful archive(s) and mark release 3 shipped here. No fourth cleanup deploy is planned. Retain all backups after sign-off.
diff --git a/spec/db/migrate/clean_up_citizen_proposal_data_spec.rb b/spec/db/migrate/clean_up_citizen_proposal_data_spec.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8fc396
--- /dev/null
+++ b/spec/db/migrate/clean_up_citizen_proposal_data_spec.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+require "rails_helper"
+require Rails.root.join("db/migrate/20260830120000_clean_up_citizen_proposal_data")
+
+describe CleanUpCitizenProposalData do
+  let(:db) { ActiveRecord::Base.connection }
+  let(:root) { Pathname(Dir.mktmpdir) }
+  let(:release2) { root.join("20260829T120000Z-#{SecureRandom.uuid}") }
+  let(:communities) { [] }
+  let(:maps) { [] }
+
+  before do
+    stub_const("CitizenProposalArchive::ROOT", root)
+    Dir.mkdir(release2)
+    allow(ENV).to receive(:fetch).and_call_original
+    allow(ENV).to receive(:fetch).with("CITIZEN_PROPOSAL_RELEASE2_ARCHIVES")
+                                 .and_return({ db.current_schema => release2.basename }.to_json)
+  end
+
+  after { FileUtils.remove_entry_secure(root) }
+
+  def write_manifest(database: db.current_database)
+    files = { "proposals.csv" => ["id,community_id", communities],
+              "linked_map_locations.csv" => ["id,proposal_id", maps] }.to_h do |filename, (header, rows)|
+      path = release2.join(filename)
+      path.write("#{header}\n" + rows.map { |r| CSV.generate_line(r) }.join)
+      [filename, { rows: rows.size, sha256: Digest::SHA256.file(path).hexdigest }]
+    end
+    release2.join("manifest.json").write({ database: database,
+                                           schema: db.current_schema,
+                                           files: files }.to_json)
+  end
+
+  it "removes exact owners (including hidden rows) and descendants, not other records with the same IDs" do
+    author = create(:user)
+    legislation = create(:legislation_proposal)
+    shared = create(:budget_investment)
+    community = Community.create!
+    communities.concat([[1, community.id], [2, shared.community_id], [3, legislation.community_id]])
+    maps << [db.select_value("INSERT INTO map_locations DEFAULT VALUES RETURNING id"), 1]
+    shared_map = db.select_value(<<~SQL)
+      INSERT INTO map_locations (investment_id) VALUES (#{shared.id}) RETURNING id
+    SQL
+    maps << [shared_map, 2]
+    topic = create(:topic, community: community)
+    comment = create(:comment, commentable: topic)
+    root_comment = create(:comment, :hidden, commentable: legislation)
+    root_comment.update_columns(commentable_type: "Proposal", commentable_id: legislation.id)
+    survivor = create(:comment, commentable: legislation)
+    create(:vote, votable: survivor)
+    create(:vote, votable: comment)
+    create(:notification, user: author, notifiable: comment)
+    keep = create(:notification, user: author, notifiable: survivor)
+    dashboard_question = create(:poll_question, :yes_no)
+    dashboard_question.poll.update_column(:related_type, "Proposal")
+    keep_question = create(:poll_question, :yes_no)
+    tag = create(:tagging).tag
+    db.execute("INSERT INTO taggings (tag_id, taggable_type, taggable_id) VALUES (#{tag.id}, 'Proposal', 1)")
+    Setting["process.proposals"] = true
+    Setting["proposal_code_prefix"] = "TEST"
+    keep_setting = Setting.find_by!(key: "proposal_code_prefix").attributes
+    write_manifest
+
+    CleanUpCitizenProposalData.new.up
+
+    expect(Comment.unscoped.where(id: [comment, root_comment, survivor]).ids).to eq([survivor.id])
+    expect(db.select_values("SELECT comment_id FROM comment_translations")).not_to include(comment.id,
+                                                                                           root_comment.id)
+    expect(Vote.where(votable: survivor)).to exist
+    expect(Vote.where(votable: comment)).not_to exist
+    expect(Notification.where(user: author).ids).to eq([keep.id])
+    expect(author.reload.notifications_count).to eq(1)
+    expect(tag.reload.taggings_count).to eq(1)
+    expect(Community.where(id: [community, shared.community_id, legislation.community_id]).ids)
+      .to match_array([shared.community_id, legislation.community_id])
+    expect(MapLocation.where(id: maps.map(&:first)).ids).to eq([maps.last.first])
+    expect(Poll::Question.unscoped.where(id: dashboard_question.id)).not_to exist
+    expect(Poll::Question::Option.where(question_id: dashboard_question.id)).not_to exist
+    expect(keep_question.reload.question_options.size).to eq(2)
+    expect(Setting.where(key: "process.proposals")).not_to exist
+    expect(Setting.find_by!(key: "proposal_code_prefix").attributes).to eq(keep_setting)
+
+    dir = (root.children - [release2]).sole
+    files = JSON.parse(dir.join("manifest.json").read).fetch("files")
+    files.each do |name, info|
+      expect(Digest::SHA256.file(dir.join(name)).hexdigest).to eq(info.fetch("sha256"))
+    end
+    expect(CSV.read(dir.join("comments.csv"),
+                    headers: true)["id"]).to include(root_comment.id.to_s, comment.id.to_s)
+    expect(CSV.read(dir.join("update_users.csv"), headers: true)["id"]).to include(author.id.to_s)
+  end
+
+  it "keeps message history, shared i18n keys and locally edited page text" do
+    message = create(:admin_notification, :sent)
+    message.update_column(:segment_recipient, "proposal_authors")
+    page = SiteCustomization::Page.find_by!(slug: "welcome_not_verified")
+    text = "Local proposals policy<li>Create new proposals</li><li>Participate in debates</li>"
+    page.update!(content: text)
+    removed = I18nContent.create!(key: "proposals.new.more_info", value: "Former text")
+    kept = I18nContent.create!(key: "proposals.form.tags_placeholder", value: "Keep this")
+    write_manifest
+    CleanUpCitizenProposalData.new.up
+
+    expect(message.reload.segment_recipient).to be_blank
+    expect(message.list_of_recipients).to be_empty
+    expect(page.reload.content).to eq("Local proposals policy<li>Participate in debates</li>")
+    expect(I18nContent.exists?(removed.id)).to be(false)
+    expect(I18nContent.translation_class.where(i18n_content_id: removed.id)).not_to exist
+    expect(kept.reload.value).to eq("Keep this")
+  end
+
+  it "never purges a shared blob when detaching a retired owner's file" do
+    image = create(:image, :budget_image)
+    attachment = image.attachment.attachment
+    blob = attachment.blob
+    bytes = blob.download
+    old_link = attachment.attributes.except("id").merge("record_type" => "Proposal")
+    ActiveStorage::Attachment.insert_all!([old_link])
+    write_manifest
+    allow(ENV).to receive(:[]).and_call_original
+    allow(ENV).to receive(:[]).with("CITIZEN_PROPOSAL_STORAGE_BACKUP").and_return("verified-test-snapshot")
+
+    CleanUpCitizenProposalData.new.up
+    expect(ActiveStorage::Attachment.where(blob_id: blob.id).ids).to eq([attachment.id])
+    expect(blob.reload.download).to eq(bytes)
+  end
+
+  it "refuses another database's archive before deletion" do
+    write_manifest(database: "wrong_database")
+    expect { CleanUpCitizenProposalData.new.up }.to raise_error(/another database\/schema/)
+  end
+
+  it "verifies the release-2 mappings, not just their directory name" do
+    write_manifest
+    release2.join("proposals.csv").open("a") { |f| f.puts "42,5" }
+    expect { CleanUpCitizenProposalData.new.up }.to raise_error(/Bad release-2 checksum/)
+  end
+
+  it "rebuilds the plan under lock and aborts on a new reference not in the fresh archive" do
+    write_manifest
+    cleanup = CitizenProposalCleanup.new(db)
+    cleanup.prepare!
+    cleanup.write!
+    db.execute("INSERT INTO activities(actionable_type, actionable_id) VALUES ('Dashboard::Action', 77)")
+    expect { cleanup.apply! }.to raise_error(/activities changed during archive/)
+    expect(Activity.where(actionable_type: "Dashboard::Action")).to exist
+  end
+end
